#
# Public-export rules for the 2026-10-31 launch.
# `export-ignore` keeps a path out of `git archive`, which is how
# scripts/public-export.sh builds the public tree. These rules do NOT rewrite
# git history: anything here is still in the private repo's history, so the
# public repository must be created from the exported tree (fresh history),
# never by flipping this repository's visibility. See docs/launch/PUBLIC-EXPORT.md.

# Line endings: keep text LF everywhere, binaries untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.wav binary
*.db binary
*.db-wal binary

# --- private material: never in the public tree -----------------------------
# Vendored Grok Bot operator material (VPS access skills, ssh MCP, private notes).
/contrib export-ignore
# Redacted secret inventories: values are <REDACTED:...> but the names, paths
# and tunnel ids are an inventory of the secret store.
*.redacted export-ignore
# The whole key-management mirror (console key routes, cloudflared config with
# the tunnel id, lock-secrets guard script).
/stack/kms export-ignore
# Index of stack/ copies: lists every secret path and the sha256 of each
# secret-holding original.
/stack/INDEX.md export-ignore

# --- build artefacts: shipped as signed release assets, not in the source tree
# (OpenSSF Scorecard "Binary-Artifacts" check).
/dist/bin export-ignore
/edge/dist export-ignore
